Given a parabola $C$: $y^{2}=2px (p > 0)$ with focus $F$, and a point $(3,m)$ on the parabola $C$ with a distance of $5$ to the focus.

$(1)$ Find the equation of the parabola $C$;

$(2)$ Draw a line $l$ through point $F$ intersecting the parabola $C$ at points $A$ and $B$. If the $y$-coordinate of the midpoint of line segment $AB$ is $-1$, find the equation of line $l$.,"<bos><start_of_turn>user

